Cosmoscope
==========

The compiled frontend is installed in /usr/share/cosmoscope.  Serve it
at the root of a dedicated website (the build uses / as its base URL).
Configure history fallback to index.html so direct links such as
/configuration work.

An nginx example is provided in examples/cosmoscope.nginx.  Replace
scope.example.com with your domain and provision a TLS certificate
(for example using Let's Encrypt); adjust ssl_certificate and
ssl_certificate_key to match.  Copy it to
/etc/nginx/sites-available/cosmoscope, enable it with a symlink in
/etc/nginx/sites-enabled, run nginx -t, and reload nginx. It
reverse-proxies /rpc to the RPC websocket.

For Caddy, copy examples/cosmoscope.Caddyfile to
/etc/caddy/cosmoscope.Caddyfile, replace scope.example.com with your
domain, and import it from /etc/caddy/Caddyfile:

    import /etc/caddy/cosmoscope.Caddyfile

Enable Cosmobot's RPC listener and set a non-empty token.  Add the
exact origin used in the browser (scheme, hostname, and port) to
rpc.allowed_browser_origins, then restart Cosmobot.  At the login
page, enter a WebSocket URL reachable from the browser and the RPC
token.  An HTTPS page needs a secure wss:// connection, usually
through your reverse proxy.
